Hi Sarah / Tom — quick technical notes ahead of the sync and the Node example attached inline.

mTLS onboarding
- We provision a customer CA that issues certs per service. Steps: CSR -> Redwood CA sign -> we install cert on Redwood side and provide verification bundle for your infra. I’ll share the onboarding doc during the call.

Embeddings / reranker (cost & latency)
- Rough ballpark: using our standard-embedding model: ~5–10ms per vector (p50) on dedicated infra; indexing + kNN lookup is another ~10–30ms depending on index size. Reranker (small cross-encoder) adds ~50–150ms per candidate. For 5k docs/day and ~3 candidates/doc, you’re well within typical Dedicated capacity — we can provide a sizing estimate after we see sample candidate counts.

Node SDK snippet (minimal)

const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood.Client({
  auth: { type: 'mtls', certPath: '/path/to/cert.pem', keyPath: '/path/to/key.pem' },
  routePolicy: { primary: 'redwood-quantized-v1', fallback: 'redwood-large-v1' }
});

async function parsePolicy(prompt, schema) {
  // Try up to 2 constrained-decode retries, then return null for human queue
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
    const resp = await client.generate({
      model: 'redwood-quantized-v1',
      prompt,
      structured_output: {
        schema, // pass full JSON schema
        constrained_decode: true,
        seed: attempt
      },
      sampling: { temperature: 0.2 }
    });

    const text = resp.output_text;
    // client-side validation (example uses AJV)
    const valid = validateWithAjv(schema, text);
    if (valid) return JSON.parse(text);
    // on failure, loop and retry with different seed (constrained decode helps)
  }
  // after retries, escalate to human review queue
  enqueueHumanReview(prompt);
  return null;
}

Notes: we recommend running a strict AJV schema check client-side to catch trailing commas/format issues before queuing repair attempts. If you prefer, we can enable server-side validation hooks that return structured error info for more targeted retries.

Attachments: small sample constrained-decode config + the schema (acme-structured-output-schema-v1.json).

See you on the sync.

